+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+Staff also ask the inverse of the veterinarian directory's question: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. The clinic answers it with a specialty directory (stated 2026-08-15). The page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each by its stored name and each with the veterinarians holding it. Every veterinarian is named in full, first name before last. A veterinarian holding no specialty is absent: the page lists specialties, not the roster `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]`. The page only reads: NG-2 stands, and nothing on it changes a specialty or a veterinarian. It is reached at its own address, and no navigation entry or link from another page is part of it (stated 2026-08-15).
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every specialty is listed by its stored name with the veterinarians holding it.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding a specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian is named first name before last, as in "Helen Leary".
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the specialty directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on it.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given every specialty the clinic knows, when the specialty directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page, with no paging controls.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the specialty directory, when it is opened, then specialties appear in name order and the veterinarians under each in last-name order.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the specialty directory, when it is rendered, then it carries the navigation every page carries, and no page links to it.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, shown as held by none.
+2. A clinic that knows no specialties yields an empty directory rather than a failure.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
